     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Ibuprofen 1600 mg by mouth four times daily is 6400 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled daily dose for prescription ibuprofen (3200 mg/day). Even at the top of the labeled range, the usual maximum is 800 mg per dose, and 1600 mg is the maximum single dose only for certain uses. At this dose, the main risks are GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, cardiovascular events, and fluid retention. The patient's normal renal and hepatic function lowers but doesn't remove those risks.\n\nPlease confirm which dose you intend. Common options:\n\n- **400\u2013800 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours** (up to 3200 mg/day), for example 800 mg PO TID or QID\n- **1600 mg PO every 8 hours** (4800 mg/day) if you intend a high-dose regimen, which would need a deliberate, documented rationale\n- Another dose or frequency\n\nIf you confirm the intended regimen, I'll enter it. If the 1600 mg QID dose is intentional, tell me the clinical indication and I'll include it in the order note."
      }
     ],
